        "generation logic in the bpfilter project.",
        "",
        "bpfilter translates packet filtering rules into BPF programs that run "
        "in the Linux kernel for every packet. Every BPF instruction eliminated "
        "from generated programs reduces per-packet latency on the hot path.",
        "",
        f"Baseline commit: {history.baseline_sha}",
        "",
        "## Register conventions",
        "",
        "r6  – pointer to the header currently being filtered on (cached across "
        "matchers within one rule; reset to BF_LOADED_HDR_NONE at every rule boundary)",
        "r7  – L3 protocol id (network-byte-order ethertype, e.g. htobe16(ETH_P_IP))",
        "r8  – L4 protocol id (e.g. IPPROTO_TCP)",
        "r10 – frame pointer (BPF stack base)",
        "r1–r5 – scratch / function args (clobbered by every kfunc/helper call)",
        "r9  – callee-saved, currently unused",
        "",
        "## BPF instruction cost (highest → lowest)",
        "",
        "1. kfunc / BPF helper calls  (bpf_dynptr_slice, map_lookup_elem, …)",
        "2. Stack loads / stores  (BPF_LDX_MEM / BPF_STX_MEM / BPF_ST_MEM via r10)",
        "3. Register ALU and MOV",
        "4. Branches  (not-taken ≈ free; mispredicted ≈ 15+ cycles)",
        "",
        "Eliminating stack accesses on the hot path is the highest-value target "
        "after reducing kfunc/helper calls.",
        "",
        "## cgen/ file inventory",
        "",
        "stub.c / stub.h      – packet-header parsing stubs (L2/L3/L4); primary hot-path target",
        "program.c / .h       – BPF program generation entry point, rule-emission loop",
        "swich.c / .h         – BPF dispatch-table (switch-case) code emitter",
        "jmp.c / .h           – forward-jump fixup management",
        "matcher/cmp.c        – comparison matchers (eq, range, bitfield, masked-address)",
        "matcher/meta.c       – meta matchers (iface, l3/l4 proto, sport/dport, probability)",
        "matcher/set.c        – set-lookup matchers (hash map and LPM trie)",
        "tc.c / xdp.c / nf.c / cgroup_skb.c  – flavor prologues and epilogues",
        "runtime.h            – bf_runtime stack layout (BF_PROG_CTX_OFF, BF_PROG_SCR_OFF)",
        "fixup.h              – fixup types (JMP_NEXT_RULE, map FDs, elfstub calls)",
        "",
        "## Task",
        "",
        "Explore src/libbpfilter/cgen/ to understand how BPF bytecode is generated, "
        "then call submit_proposal with ONE concrete optimization. Focus on changes "
        "that reduce the number or cost of BPF instructions in the hot path. "
        "Never target cgroup_sock_addr programs — no benchmarks exist for them. "
        "Use list_dir, read_file, and grep as needed.",
    ]

    if recent_commits:
        parts += [
            "",
            "## Already implemented — do not reproduce these",
            "",
            recent_commits,
        ]

    if config.hint:
        parts += [
            "",
            "## Hint",
            "",
            config.hint,
            "",
            "This is a direction to explore, not a constraint.",
        ]

    if history.attempts:
        parts += [
            "",
            "## Previous attempts this run — do not repeat these ideas",
            "",
        ]
        for a in history.attempts:
            bm_summary = ""
            if a.benchmark_results:
                avg = sum(r["delta_time_pct"] for r in a.benchmark_results) / len(
                    a.benchmark_results
                )
                bm_summary = f"  (avg Δtime: {avg:+.1f}%)"
            delta_info = (
                f" [Δinsn: {a.proposal.estimated_insn_delta:+d}]"
                if a.proposal.estimated_insn_delta
                else ""
            )
            target_info = (
                f"\n  Target: {a.proposal.target_function}"
                if a.proposal.target_function
                else ""
            )
            parts.append(
                f"- #{a.id} [{a.status.value}]{bm_summary}{delta_info}{target_info}\n"
                f"  Reasoning: {a.proposal.reasoning.strip()}\n"
                f"  Plan: {a.proposal.implementation_plan.strip()}"
            )

    if prior_attempts:
        parts += [
            "",
            "## Attempts from prior runs — do not repeat these ideas",
            "",
        ]
        for a in prior_attempts:
            target_info = (
                f" [{a.proposal.target_function}]"
                if a.proposal.target_function
                else ""
            )
            parts.append(
                f"- [{a.status.value}]{target_info} "
                f"{a.proposal.reasoning[:200].strip()}"
            )

    return "\n".join(parts)


